"Id_42" <id.fortytwo@gmail.com> wrote:
>I was recently trying to make a super-awesome +7 Mjollnir by means of
>enchanting, unenchanting, re-enchanting, etc. Got it to +5, read a
>blessed scroll, and it only went to +6- so, okay, no problem, I
>happened to have a cursed scroll on me. Read that, and immediately read
>another blessed scroll. "Your Mjollnir glows violently blue for a while
>and then evaporates."

Let's be clear on this: the +7 Mjollnir is not measurably superior (in
the hands of a high-level high-luck character) to the +6 Mjollnir.

It gets one more point of to-hit bonus (big deal; a 14th-level character
with maxed luck already has a to-hit bonus of +27 before considering
weapon skills, strength, dexterity, and weapon bonuses; you need three
points from any source to achieve 100% accuracy against any opponent
except a well-equipped mplayer) and does one more point of damage (big
deal; this means it does 9-37 instead of 8-36).

This is why I never bother pissing about with applying disenchantment
effects to my artifacts. If I get +7, it's groovy gravy. If I get +6,
it's still no damn slop.
